# workflows/molab/.env.example -- copy to workflows/molab/.env and fill in.
#
# env.sh sources the first of ${MOLAB_ENV_FILE}, workflows/molab/.env and the
# .env one level above the checkout (/marimo/.env) that exists. The real .env is
# gitignored: it holds credentials, and this repo's .gitignore does not
# otherwise cover it.
#
#   cp workflows/molab/.env.example workflows/molab/.env
#   $EDITOR workflows/molab/.env
#   source workflows/molab/env.sh

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub token, for pushing the working branch. molab has no persistent disk,
# so commits that live only on the box are lost when the session ends.
# Needs `repo` scope (or `public_repo` for a public fork). Create at
# https://github.com/settings/tokens
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...

# The GitHub account the token belongs to. Not a secret, and no script here
# reads it: env.sh's credential helper sends the token as x-access-token.
# GITHUB_USER=emattei

# ── The molab bucket (setup_molab.sh, sync_to_gcs.sh) ────────────────────────
# Private: the d0 test data (chrombpnet/test_data_d0/{config,inputs}/), which
# setup_molab.sh fetches, and the results, commits and config sync_to_gcs.sh
# writes under MOLAB_GCS_PREFIX. GCP_SA_JSON is the service-account key file's
# CONTENTS as one quoted line of JSON, not a path. gcs.sh mints tokens from it
# with openssl and never writes it to disk. Never commit a real key.
# GCP_BUCKET="broad-nnfc-molab"
# GCP_SA_JSON='{"type":"service_account","client_email":"...","private_key":"<PEM, newlines as \\n>","...":"..."}'

# Where sync_to_gcs.sh keeps results/ and run_step.sh restores them from
# (default chrombpnet/test_data_d0). Give a chrombpnet 2.x run its OWN prefix,
# together with its own output_dir in the dataset config: the restore plus
# run_step.sh's skip check would otherwise treat the 1.x results as done.
# MOLAB_GCS_PREFIX=chrombpnet/test_data_d0_cbp2

# ── Dataset ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATASET=d0
# A copy of the fetched config with a fresh output_dir, for a 2.x run. A copy
# under another name, because setup_molab.sh re-fetches config/config.yaml
# from the bucket and replaces a local edit of it.
# DATASET_CONFIG=/marimo/data/test_data_d0/config/config.cbp2.yaml
# REFERENCE_ROOT=/marimo/data/references

# ── Box-specific ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The REAL core count. The box reports the host's (20+), not the slice you get.
# MOLAB_CPUS=4

# Cap this pipeline's share of the GPU (a fraction of the card's TOTAL memory)
# when other jobs use it too. Unset: it may use the whole card.
# XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_MEM_FRACTION=0.25

# The chrombpnet 2.x checkout and environment (defaults shown). cuda12 is the
# fallback for NVIDIA drivers older than 580.
# CHROMBPNET_REPO=/marimo/chrombpnet-igvf
# CHROMBPNET_PIXI_ENV=cuda13
